        "description": "Resembles SQL injection: a user-supplied query-string value `q` (request.GET.get('q')) is fed directly into a database filter that searches name and email. It is actually safe because it uses the Django ORM QuerySet API with Q(name__icontains=q) | Q(billing_contact_email__icontains=q); the value is bound as a parameter by the ORM, never string-concatenated into raw SQL, so no injection is possible. No .raw(), .extra(), or cursor.execute with f-strings is involved."
