        "description": "Resembles an IDOR/BOLA: the view takes a `pk` straight from the URL and calls get_object_or_404(Organization, pk=pk), a classic user-controlled-resource-id pattern. It is actually safe because immediately after fetching it enforces ownership via `if not _org_access(request, org): return redirect('dashboard')`, and _org_access delegates to request.user.can_access_organization(org), which scopes by role (account_manager==self, assigned support agent, or customer's own organization). Access is denied for non-owners, so this is not a broken object-level authorization flaw."
